A table whose columns are state takes a new count when they change. Fyne
lays a table out as a grid, whose column count is container.NewGridWithColumns'
argument: no method of a Container sets it again, so the write the columns'
change makes was answered as the constructor's (a constructor-only prop) and
reached nothing, and a column added fell to the next row.
fynelayout.SetGridColumns is the grid's setter, a function since Fyne gives
none (a Spec Setter's `fn`), and the click that adds a column calls it.

pkg/go/fynelayout's TestSetGridColumnsLaysOutThatManyToARow lays out with it.
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        fyne
    }
}

component page ui.node {
    var cols = ["a", "b"]
    ui.button(text="more", @click {
        cols.push("c")
    })
    ui.table(columns=cols, rows=[])
}

ui.window {
    page()
}
-- out/go/fyne/model.go --
